    "authors_reviews": [
      {
        "position": 1,
        "title": "Levels Up My Tub",
        "text": "I have 2 active herding mix dogs and we do a lot of stuff outdoors so the need arises frequently to have to bathe them. I only have a regular sized bathtub/shower with a fixed shower head so bathing them at home has always been a bit annoying and I found myself going to self bathing places instead, but that does add up in cost especially with 2 of them. I wanted this water pump mostly for at home use just to make that process easier and save me money in the long run.Assembling this whole thing is very easy. It is pretty self explanatory how it all goes together. The water pressure is good, don't expect anything too crazy because it isn't that high powered. But it is certainly enough to rinse the shampoo off and is a big upgrade to me using a cup to pour water over them. I especially like to see the temperature being displayed. Admittedly, that is less important at home where I can control the water temperature easily but I think it will be very helpful for using it in the yard or out adventuring to make sure my sweet dogs are as comfortable as possible.Make sure that the pump is fully submerged or you will run into problems quickly!This pump is pretty small and it comes with a convenient mesh carry bag so it be taken with you on adventures. Now, I am unlikely to be using something like this while camping. But, I do think it will come on handy on day trips when I can use fresh water to rinse to rinse river water off my dogs after a play session when they are already wet. Also, this summer I plan to use it in the yard in our kiddie pools to help rinse dogs and keep them cool in the heat.I was pretty happy with the ease of use of this pump and the overall quality. I was a little skeptical when I got it, but I do like it. Just remember, don't expect like a garden hose level of pressure and make sure to always keep the pump submerged and only use it with fresh water, not mucky water that will clog it quickly. It seems like a great addition to the at home bathing supplies of an adventure dog!",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "June 26, 2026",
        "author": "Kara",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AFS2R3BSQFCFRJ6QHQCQXLDJNRFA?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/5d0bd521-34d9-418d-a257-0b3db9342d58._CR62%2C0%2C375%2C375_SX460_SX48_.jpg",
        "helpful_votes": "2 people found this helpful"
      },
      {
        "position": 2,
        "title": "Works Well!",
        "text": "I have a Bichon, born white, but he prefers mud colored hair and as stinky as he can get... rolling on stink bugs, goose poop, etc is a favorite activity. We prefer not to bring him in our tub with all these {not} delightful things on him. Enter, this outdoor shower, the ability to use warmish water in the outside setting is very goodA couple observations. This shower provides the water flow and the easy use for our purpose. It is pretty much lightweight, good size to hold in hand and wash the dog. The quality seems reasonable and with care, as long as the pump holds up, it should, with care, last.A couple technical issues: the pump has to be full submerged so a bucket of water doesn't last very far. It take about 3 buckets to get my small dog wet, shampooed and rinsed and keeping the pump under water the whole time is kind of tricky. We don't have outside faucet, so that means carrying out buckets of water before starting, if we start and refill bucket we then have to chase the {wet} dog who is covered in mud again. The pump is kind of big in the bucket, making quite a bit of the water unusable without refill.I'm not sure about the price, it seems reasonable, but I have never purchased one of the outdoor showers to compare it to.I do think it is a good product and when we work out the issue of having enough water available to keep constant flow I will be really happy. Maybe a kid pool that I leave in the sun to warm the water, then just another bucket for final rinse would work.",
        "rating": 4,
        "date": "July 18, 2026",
        "author": "Linda Thinks",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AFVAQKTYUR4Q324G7DURJHAHAYJQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "helpful_votes": "One person found this helpful"
      },
      {
        "position": 3,
        "title": "Good, Portable Dog Shower with Easy Setup",
        "text": "I ordered this portable dog shower because I needed to improve the process I use for bathing my two dogs. Now, instead of dumping water on them to rinse them, I can make their bath times a little more pleasant and efficient by rinsing them with an even, steady flow of water.Setting up the shower is very easy. I just attached the hose to the pump, made sure the pump was completely submerged in water, and turned the pump on to start the shower. I liked that the pump is quiet and shows both the remaining battery percentage as well as the water temperature. Sometimes, while I’m bathing my dogs, I get a little worried that I’m using water that is too hot or too cold, so being able to see the water temperature right there on the pump is reassuring.So far I haven’t experienced any problems using this dog shower. It’s a pretty simple thing to use and it works as advertised. The pump itself feels pretty durable and seems like it’ll keep working well for a while to come. I would recommend this to others who need a quick and easy way to bathe a pet.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "June 22, 2026",
